// ============================================================
// .markdownlint.jsonc (ALL-REPOS)
// ============================================================
// Updated: 2026-10-11
//
// WHAT: A configuration file for checking Markdown documentation.
//       Markdown is a lightweight format for writing documentation.
//       JSONC is JSON with comments, allowing rules to be explained.
//       This file tells markdownlint which formatting rules to apply.
//
// WHEN: Use in professional projects containing README.md, CHANGELOG.md,
//       documentation pages, or other Markdown files.
//
// WHY: Professional documentation should be consistent, readable,
//      and easy to maintain. Automated linting helps identify common
//      formatting problems before documentation is shared or published.
//      Some rules are relaxed to support practical documentation styles.
//
// HOW: The VS Code markdownlint extension reads this configuration
//      and identifies potential problems while editing Markdown files.
//      Rules set to false are disabled; other default rules remain enabled.
//      Project maintainers may also run markdownlint-cli2 separately.
//
// SKILLS: Markdown, JSONC, documentation quality, linting,
//         automated validation, and professional communication.
//
// TOOLS: The VS Code markdownlint extension checks Markdown files.
//        Students do not need Node.js or npx to use the extension.
//        Maintainers may optionally use markdownlint-cli2 with npx.
//
// REQ: Professional repositories SHOULD maintain consistent Markdown.
// REQ: Disabled rules SHOULD have documented reasons.
//
// OBS: This file configures linting but does not modify Markdown files.
// OBS: Disabled rules do not prevent other Markdown checks from running.
//
// SEE: https://github.com/DavidAnson/markdownlint
// ============================================================
{
  "MD013": false, // Allow long lines.
  "MD024": false, // Allow repeated headings in different sections.
  "MD025": false, // Allow multiple top-level headings.
  "MD026": false, // Allow punctuation at the end of headings.
  "MD033": false, // Allow inline HTML in Markdown.
  "MD034": false, // Allow URLs without Markdown link syntax.
  "MD041": false, // Allow content before the first heading.
  "MD060": false  // Allow different Markdown table formatting styles.
}
